sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Nakamasu et al. (2009) 3-variable zebrafish pigment-cell reaction-diffusion network, laser-ablation polarity & leopard (cx41.8) spot-to-stripe morphospace — MorphoEval overall 47.4/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py` (overall weighted score: 49.8 / 100). The v1 script computes the linear dispersion curve sigma(k) of the 3-variable Nakamasu et al. (2009) melanophore-xanthophore-factor matrix J0 - k^2 D (k_c = 3.41, lambda_c = 1.84), but approximates spatial stripes via a static cosine formula (`synthesize_cosine_stripes`) rather than numerically integrating the nonlinear 3-species piecewise-saturated reaction-diffusion PDE for (u, v, w) with zero-flux Neumann boundaries; omits in silico laser-ablation regeneration and xanthophore-depletion survival collapse (Nakamasu 2009 Figs. 2-3); omits the leopard (cx41.8) spot-to-labyrinth-to-stripe morphospace sweep and dual negative controls; does not load or segment the vendored Danio rerio specimen photograph; and returns only 2 analytical measurements without CLI parameter flags. Overall 47.4/100 (faithfulness 40.6, reproducibility 63.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 52, Morphological realism / specimen match 28, Parameter expressivity 44, Morphometric validation 44, Source and data traceability 62, Code-to-model traceability 58, Reproducibility package 68. Output judged: docs/media/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes_comparison.png: rendered output of 2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py at 8871db0, image/png, 71468 B, 1287×506 px, artifact_sha256 7e46a54e2f714ffd53caae044f5a706fdcb564aaf6b81e0178f41774fbd69538 (sha256 7e46a54e2f714ffd53caae044f5a706fdcb564aaf6b81e0178f41774fbd69538), spec_fingerprint e325ab05dbc489df59ad15e0ad7e5ce094c3a9ea9e524b654d3adbb036c29214. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: e325ab05dbc489df59ad15e0ad7e5ce094c3a9ea9e524b654d3adbb036c29214; artifact_sha256: 7e46a54e2f714ffd53caae044f5a706fdcb564aaf6b81e0178f41774fbd69538; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/danio_rerio_specimen.jpg=850b2d4a94c7cbcb..., datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/scout_manifest.json=d19df92d7c80de8a..., datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes_reference.json=fcc1809ce2e992bc...}." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Implement dual formal negative controls around the homogeneous steady state: (1) equal-diffusion control D_w = D_u = D_v = 0.02 (testing Lean Theorem 3), and (2) ablated short-range mutual repulsion b_u = a_v = 0.0 (testing Lean Theorem 1 where det J_uv > 0 prevents pigment segregation).",
            "remediation needed: Load and SHA-256-verify `datasets/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes_reference.json`, `danio_rerio_specimen.jpg`, `scout_manifest.json`, and `paper_citations.bib`; segment the dark melanophore stripes and yellow/iridescent interstripes from `danio_rerio_specimen.jpg`; expose full CLI flags; expand `measure_morphoeval()` to 8 reference-backed morphometrics; and render an 8-panel comparison PNG and 6-frame growth GIF.",
            "remediation needed: Replace `synthesize_cosine_stripes` with a genuine 2D nonlinear 3-species (u, v, w) reaction-diffusion PDE solver (spectral DCT-II IMEX with zero-flux Neumann boundary conditions and piecewise-saturating synthesis rates) modeling wild-type horizontal myoseptum-guided stripes, unguided labyrinthine stripes, and *leopard* (cx41.8) mutant spot regimes.",
            "remediation needed: Simulate Nakamasu et al. (2009) Figs. 2-3 laser-ablation experiments in silico: (1) selective xanthophore interstripe ablation demonstrating melanophore stripe survival collapse when long-range w support is removed, and (2) rectangular stripe ablation demonstrating directional horizontal stripe regeneration vs isotropic spot/labyrinth fill-in." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.474"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (Slot 007 autonomous loop assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

